# Legal data and unverifiable content (non-negotiable)

## Never invent or complete
SIRET/SIREN, hosting provider identity, Formspree form ID, payment links, IBAN,
VAT number, postal address, or any other legal or official data. Never use an
example value that could be mistaken for a real one.

## Placeholder convention
- In visible text: `[À COMPLÉTER : <what is needed>]`
- In code: a comment `TODO-OWNER: <what is needed>` at the exact place to fill.
- Every placeholder must be reported to the user in your reply.
- Publication is blocked while any of these strings remains: `VOTRE_`, `À COMPLÉTER`, `TODO-OWNER`, `XXXX`. Say so when you finish a task.

## Testimonials
The unverifiable testimonials were removed from the home page by owner decision
(2026-09-20). Do not put them back, edit old copies, or add new ones without
a new decision from the owner.

## Social links
Two conflicting sets exist (Pinterest/Facebook vs Instagram/Facebook). Ask which are real. Do not pick.

## Legal pages (mentions légales, CGV, privacy policy)
- Do not rewrite legal wording.
- You may remove navigation links to the shop.
- Flag anything inconsistent with the changes: mentions of the shop, cart, Stripe, PayPal, bank transfer; missing mention of Formspree (contact form) or of third-party map tiles (Leaflet). Let the owner decide, ideally with a qualified person. You are not a lawyer.

## Artwork detail pages
`oeuvres/*.html` exist in this project. Check locally (file list, not "the live site")
whether each page referenced in the sitemap and in the JS `works` data actually exists,
and whether its slug matches the corresponding image/data filename. Report every
mismatch you find instead of guessing which name is correct. Do not delete or rename
files yourself — flag and wait.
